            <ArticleTitle>Intracranial subdural hygroma after Le Fort I osteotomy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>727-31</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.joms.2014.10.023</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0278-2391(14)01622-X</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Various intra- and postoperative complications have been well-documented after Le Fort I osteotomies; however, an intracranial subdural hygroma has not yet been reported in oral and maxillofacial studies. We report a unique case of an intracranial subdural hygroma requiring neurosurgical intervention after Le Fort I advancement.</AbstractText>
